WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Act 11: "Oh, I Think I Love Classical Ballet"

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.980
<b><b>Boys Summer Class
Day 8: Last Day</b></b>

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:10.480
Some of you may have performed 
the <i>Swan Lake</i> Siegfried variation before

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.480
<b>Variation Performances</b>

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.860
at a competition or elsewhere.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.010
Man, I knew it. Jumpei and Luou didn't show.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.380
What's important is not difficult technique.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:23.580
What we want is the dignity of a prince, 
a beautiful shape, and precision.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.200
If that's all it takes to keep 
them from performin',

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.500
then that's the extent of their resolve.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.640
Go ahead, Nakamura-sensei.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.500
<b>Oikawa Haruka Ballet School SS Class</b>

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.500
We will now decide the order...

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.500
<b>Confirmed Scholarship Recipient</b>

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:50.720
<i>Damn it, this is a charade!</i>

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.200
You suck at this!

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:57.570
You liar!

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:01.700
<i>Liar!</i>

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.970
<i>I thought you would only look 
at me, no matter what.</i>

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:12.090
<i>I'll become a princess</i>

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.000
<i>and protect you forever.</i>

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:16.840
<i>Liar.</i>

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:19.620
<i>I believed you.</i>

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:22.900
Ни пуха ни пера.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.610
<i>Even if I can do ballet,</i>

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.600
<i>nobody's looking at </i>me<i>!</i>

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.500
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.290
<i>I'm the one who's in the way.</i>

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.010
<i>It's always me!</i>

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.970
<i>I'm Rothbart, through and through!</i>

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:00.220
<i>I'm a mass of hatred 
that exists for no reason.</i>

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.970
<i>Come back to life, like you did back then...</i>

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.720
<i>So I can kill you again!</i>

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.230
Hey...

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.320
What're you doing?

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:15.590
Come back to life...

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:20.740
<i>Damn it...</i>

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.530
<i>I can't stand up again.</i>

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:32.000
Tombé, pas de bourrée, glissade, jeté...

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:38.260
Tombé, pas de bourrée, glissade, jeté...

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:38.840
To...

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.760
I want you to look at me...

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:43.010
I'll dance,

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:50.140
so please, give Rothbart—give <i>me</i>—wings...

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.900
Kozuru-san's doing great today.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.650
She went for a walk with her 
grandson this morning.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.400
Oh, there they are.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:02.070
Wh-What's going on?

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.560
<i>Oh...</i>

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.060
<i>Back then, I was satisfied with just myself.</i>

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.700
<i>I forgot myself,</i>

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.370
<i>using this body that you made.</i>

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.910
Oh, I hate dancers who have the wrong idea.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:55.380
In classical ballet, there is 
no need for individuality.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.600
<i>Look at me...</i>

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.740
<i>Going against your will...</i>

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.100
<i>Distorted...</i>

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:02.770
<i>Look! Look!</i>

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:06.920
<i>Look...</i>

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:09.220
<i>at me!</i>

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:41.560
Huh?

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:44.740
What was that dance?

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.480
Excellent!

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:05.490
Mazuru-chan, you really are very good!

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.310
Excellent!

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:17.980
What... am I?

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.600
К чёрту.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:31.870
Why...

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:34.600
do you know that?

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:37.380
You taught it to me.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.360
Did I?

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:46.360
I can dance now because of
 that time we spent together.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:49.870
You're my dream.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:51.880
Now...

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:53.870
and in the future...

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:55.950
Forever...

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:04.590
I want you to let me stay by your side 
and help you, so you can keep dancing.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:15.640
Jumpei.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:19.210
Thanks.

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:21.400
Sorry.

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:23.930
The rest of this is a family matter.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.700
Besides, I don't think you need 
to play at being friends.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:33.030
Believe in your gut from now on, too.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:36.770
Because for you, that's what's correct.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.020
Luou.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:52.800
I was cursed by the same person you were.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:58.350
And I know that you have 
the power to rise above that.

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:04.610
I don't think there's anyone more 
qualified to teach you right now.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:09.080
I want you to let me help you 
change the curse into magic.

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:11.880
No.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:15.500
Oh, really?! Then I won't give you a choice!

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:19.990
Stop... let go! I can't breathe! Stop...

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:19.540
Why's it okay for Miyako, but not for me?!

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.670
I'm your guardian for now, so you'd better...

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:21.670
That hurts...

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.260
Oh, this guy's good!

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:39.930
He feels very noble.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.960
He really is good, isn't he?

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:46.250
He's smart, knows himself, and has ambition.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:48.540
He'll get even better.

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.940
<i>Fukuoka Yudai-san's grand style</i>

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:56.620
<i>and strong technique that 
brings out a manly gallantry...</i>

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:00.460
<i>Akimoto Yasuomi-san's beautiful arms,</i>

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:02.880
<i>the simple accuracy of his footwork,</i>

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:05.580
<i>and his academic but elegant presentation...</i>

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:10.540
Damn it, if this were <i>Don Quixote's</i> 
Basilio, I don't think I'd lose...

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:16.690
<i>Yeah, Yamato, there's a better school 
and company out there for ya.</i>

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:20.600
<i>As you hope, that might be overseas...</i>

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.810
<i>But this is Oikawa.</i>

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:30.190
Japanese dancers are as skilled 
as dancers around the world.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:34.840
First, Oikawa needs to become a
company overseas dancers want to join.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:39.820
I want you to become a principal 
who will lead that Oikawa.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:43.450
<i>My future started to take shape.</i>

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:56.020
<i>The elegance of a traditional prince</i>

00:08:56.020 --> 00:09:01.050
<i>drawn out by Izawa Shun-san's 
extraordinary physique!</i>

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.650
So cool!

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:12.360
<i>I'm the type Oikawa wants.</i>

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.150
<i>I'm the best fit for Oikawa.</i>

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:19.720
Wow, I could feel his pure happiness 
at the princess coming to meet him.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:23.160
How do ya hide that mean streak of yours?

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:28.160
I'm not like you. I don't dance 
with my personality or emotions.

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:30.450
I'm the type who does research

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:33.870
and then applies techniques 
to express emotions.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:35.130
I'm a liar.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:40.130
I mean, I want to dance more.

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.520
<i>I don't want to give this up!</i>

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:46.330
And that concludes the performances.

00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:51.120
Everyone, good work these past eight days.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:53.400
You were all wonderful.

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:59.610
I hope this summer school session 
will be of use to you in the future.

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:04.780
The scholarship recipient 
will be contacted shortly.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.480
Reverence.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.290
Misaki's gonna get the scholarship, right?

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:12.830
Yeah...

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:16.540
Thank you very much!

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:31.430
I made it...

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:32.940
Jumpei?

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.510
You did <i>not</i> make it.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:39.050
Huh?

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:40.900
Oh, wait!

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:43.630
Hang on! I can start dancing right away.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:47.350
Good thing I put this on 
underneath just in case!

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:49.080
Hang on!

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:50.640
Just a minute!

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:51.450
Watch me!

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:52.550
Stop, Murao!

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:54.040
Please watch!

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:56.790
Tsumamura-san, music, please!

00:10:57.070 --> 00:10:58.050
Murao!

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.810
Oh, shit! Ayako-san's pissed!

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:05.090
Jumpei-kun, do this some other day!

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:06.430
This is just gonna backfire!

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:08.430
Tsumamura-san, please!

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:19.800
Thanks!

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:22.150
What?! He's really gonna dance?!

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:26.360
He's totally out of breath 
and dripping sweat...

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:29.320
Hey, at least wipe the floor.

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:30.550
You'll slip!

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:47.620
<i>The atmosphere...</i>

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.470
<i>He changed it with one jump...</i>

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:53.770
L-Look, this is what I was talking about!

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:54.650
Please watch!

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:55.730
I <i>am</i> watching.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:57.600
Murao's charisma!

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:00.870
Well, compared to the ballet festival,

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:03.920
he at least understands each movement

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:06.580
and is attempting to perform 
each movement correctly.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:09.660
Doesn't it seem like he's 
barely touching the floor?

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:13.460
<i>He's floating around in a way 
that doesn't seem very princely.</i>

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.610
The prince's joy is spreading out from him.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:18.820
<i>Isn't he just overacting?</i>

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:22.010
He looks so carefree. It's fun to watch.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.990
<i>He's </i>too<i> carefree. He isn't 
hitting the right positions.</i>

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:29.080
Does it look like that since he's 
got long arms and legs? Lucky.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:31.730
<i>It's because they're long that 
it's easier to see small mistakes.</i>

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:34.330
<i>See? His wrist is too bent.</i>

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.180
<i>A shaky landing.</i>

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:39.430
Hmm... He didn't have a solid landing,

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:43.020
and there were times his knees, 
toes, and turnout weren't very good.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:46.810
But then, there are times he's 
thinking too much about the details,

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:50.010
and it's making his movements stiff.

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:54.780
<i>Seriously. He's just beginner, after all.</i>

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:58.790
The movements haven't 
become second nature yet.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:05.230
But now and then, there's suddenly 
a moment that captivates you.

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:07.800
<i>Yeah, that's it.</i>

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:14.300
<i>A scrap of that proper Prince 
Siegfried he's going for...</i>

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:19.730
<i>The image of what he could do if he 
just had the technique to do it...</i>

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:22.220
<i>There's that sense of expectation!</i>

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:27.850
<i>Odette!</i>

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.830
<i>I can't believe </i>you<i> would come to </i>me<i>!</i>

00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:34.240
<i>It makes me giddy when our 
hearts are one like that!</i>

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:36.160
<i>This...</i>

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.950
<i>It's like something's suddenly appearing...</i>

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:39.120
<i>Get it?</i>

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:39.870
<i>Know what I mean?</i>

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:44.730
<i>I want to throw myself at you 
and tell you everything!</i>

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:47.660
<i>But I can't.</i>

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:49.380
<i>That's not dignified.</i>

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:53.710
<i>With only my one layer of skin, I have to 
keep all my emotions from bursting out.</i>

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:56.230
<i>I'll gather them all into a certain shape,</i>

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:58.940
<i>and even give off an air of composure...</i>

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:06.210
<i>Oh, I think I love classical ballet...</i>

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:09.190
Doesn't he seem more princely?

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.690
Oh, no...

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:31.530
<i>That's right.</i>

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:35.690
<i>You were Rothbart's...</i>

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:40.060
<i>Part of me thought it'd turn out like this...</i>

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:43.060
Hey, Jumpei! What're ya doin'?

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:44.750
The music's about to end!

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:55.360
What?! He's doing different choreography?!

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:57.620
Is he just desperate 'cause he fell?

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:02.120
What happened? Where's the prince's joy?

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.870
<i>You're kidding. Is this guy an idiot?</i>

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:08.490
This is what Mommy hates the most—

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.870
What was that for, Sis?

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:13.880
<i>Does this mean I have a chance?</i>

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:15.520
No...

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:20.240
He felt signs of the tragedy of Odile...

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:21.890
Because of his fall!

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:27.590
<i>Don't tell me he's improvising </i>that<i>?</i>

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:51.100
Oh, he's back to the happy Siegfried!

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:56.600
But with that part in the middle 
where the spell was almost broken,

00:15:56.600 --> 00:16:00.720
it makes the happy jumping 
and turning look sad.

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:03.140
By adding emotional ups and downs,

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:07.390
he was able to make a story 
in even that short variation.

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:09.590
C'mon, ain't that givin' him too much credit?

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:12.400
It's not like he needs to do that, anyway...

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:15.670
Huh?! Why are ya cryin'?!

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:18.490
Putting aside whether 
it's necessary or correct,

00:16:19.230 --> 00:16:21.990
it's my first time seeing 
a variation like this.

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:25.660
Jumpei-kun doesn't have 
any experience, but...

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:33.660
<i>His sensibilities, physical ability, 
physique, and intuition...</i>

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:37.610
All the things you can't get 
through hard work...

00:16:38.570 --> 00:16:40.460
He's got them all.

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.490
Talent...

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:53.310
really is cruel...

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:17.760
<i>This weird atmosphere again, huh?</i>

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:25.990
Wow!

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:27.170
That was amazing, Murao!

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:28.520
I got goosebumps!

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:31.640
Man, you piss me off!

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:33.590
Why's Kotobuki crying?!

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:37.150
You really are aggravating!

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:40.650
<i>I can't clap... for that...</i>

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:42.450
<i>What's with him?</i>

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:45.190
<i>He does crazy things, 
and he's a terrible dancer.</i>

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:47.160
<i>But... yeah...</i>

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:49.410
<i>I felt it back then.</i>

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:50.910
<i>The overflowing feeling of elation!</i>

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:53.160
<i>What is this?</i>

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:55.620
<i>This... isn't fair!</i>

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:04.300
Did you stop me to show me that?

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:08.430
Did you really think I'd want to 
see something like that?

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:10.490
You even changed the choreography.

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:12.670
I had no choice!

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:14.800
I came to my senses for a second!

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:17.250
<i>It wasn't him trying to cover up his fall?</i>

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:20.320
<i>It was because Siegfried made him do it?</i>

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:23.270
Of course you had a choice.

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:27.010
Are you saying that your choreography 
is better than Petipa's?

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:28.000
N-No...

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.470
Tsumamura-san, when 
the choreography changed,

00:18:30.470 --> 00:18:33.350
why did you change the tone 
of your playing just for him?

00:18:33.350 --> 00:18:35.570
You need to remain impartial.

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:39.340
I'm sorry. I wasn't trying to change it.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:43.500
But I was caught up in the 
atmosphere and couldn't help it.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:45.870
It's been years since that's happened!

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:51.600
Murao! Did you learn that 
contemporary part from Godai-sensei?

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:53.850
Huh? Oh, no, um...

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:56.600
I just copy ballet videos and stuff a lot...

00:18:56.600 --> 00:19:00.610
So one of those movements 
came out all of a sudden and...

00:19:01.050 --> 00:19:02.770
Anyway, sorry.

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:07.530
I don't really know the difference between, 
like, "contemporary" and ballet...

00:19:07.530 --> 00:19:11.890
Yes, I do acknowledge that 
you have some kind of talent.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:14.400
However,

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:19.120
your temperament is really 
 not suited for classical ballet.

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:24.310
Since the core of Oikawa is classical ballet,

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:29.770
it would be better for you to 
go back to Godai Ballet Studio.

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:34.230
Yes.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:42.910
It's true that Godai-sensei enjoys 
that part of me and recognizes it.

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:45.190
The first time you danced here,

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:47.700
I also saw the same pipe dream for you!

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:51.870
That's why I broke it off 
with them and came here!

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:57.830
Please whip me into shape, 
starting with the basics, at Oikawa!

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:07.840
Can I take that to mean

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:13.310
that you have severed relations 
with Godai Ballet Studio?

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:15.630
Yes.

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:17.850
Are you prepared to throw 
away your ego and your past,

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:22.060
and follow the Oikawa way 100%?

00:20:23.190 --> 00:20:24.360
Yes!

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:32.090
Nakamura-sensei, lend him some clothes.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:37.080
Murao-kun, when you have finished 
changing, come to the office.

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:43.800
The scholarship will go to Murao-kun.

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:51.020
Jumpei-kun!

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:53.900
Congrats!

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:56.560
You made me nervous, too!

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:59.930
Lucky! You got the scholarship! 
For the SS class!

00:20:59.930 --> 00:21:02.310
Yeah, that's great!

00:21:02.310 --> 00:21:04.320
You're seriously too amazing!

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:06.910
Jumpei!

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.280
That's amazing!

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:09.640
Here, use this.

00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:14.510
Oh, so that's what you 
look like when you smile.

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:18.550
You've got a low boiling point, little lady!

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:20.460
Hey!

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:25.560
It's over...

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:26.640
All of it.

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:29.450
You'd better work hard.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:32.400
Don't give up!

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:38.400
But I didn't get the scholarship.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.260
My parents will make me quit!

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:43.390
Don't quit!

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:11.680
<b>October 6
(Thursday)</b>

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:12.430
<b>Junior High School
Japanese 2</b>

00:22:15.350 --> 00:22:17.520
<b>Oikawa Ballet School</b>

00:22:24.210 --> 00:22:26.780
Jumpei's dancing <i>again</i>.

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:31.030
Why ballet?

00:22:38.930 --> 00:22:41.640
<i>I don't know how to answer when asked "why."</i>

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:44.830
<i>Because I wanna dance?</i>

00:22:45.880 --> 00:22:48.270
<i>Because I wanna get better!</i>

00:22:49.350 --> 00:22:51.300
<i>Because the stars will explode!</i>

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:12.300
<i>Tingle...</i>

00:23:12.900 --> 00:23:14.190
<i>Sparkle...</i>

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:16.410
<i>Boom!</i>

00:23:17.410 --> 00:23:21.160
<i>How can I stop?!</i>
